sistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.11432655723547953,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.023933548601724853,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":26.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05972347825350166,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12703247480403135,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03154,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":21.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"SI-BONE, Inc., a medical device company, develops procedural solutions for compromised bone, grounded in expertise in biomechanical design and anatomy-specific applications in the United States and internationally. It offers a series of patented titanium implants and the instruments used to implant them, as well as implantable bone products. The company also provides IFUSE, a triangular titanium implant with a triangular cross-section and porous surface that stabilizes the joint and facilitates the biological fixation of the bone onto the implant to drive fusion; IFUSE 3D, a triangular titanium implant with a porous surface and fenestrated design to self-harvest bone; IFUSE BONE, which supports and augments the patient's own bone tissue in orthopedic procedures; IFUSE TORQ, an additively-manufactured threaded implant designed to allow for osteointegration, or incorporation of the bone into the implant's porous surface and structure; IFUSE BEDROCK GRANITE, an implant with a machined titanium core and a tulip that attaches to the rod and provides fusion and fixation to the sacroiliac joint as a foundational element for segmental spinal fusion; and IFUSE TORQ TNT, a porous threaded design with lengths capable of spanning the posterior pelvis, passing through the ipsilateral ilium, sacrum, and through the contralateral ilium. The company markets its products primarily with a direct sales force, as well as through third-party sales agents and resellers. SI-BONE, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Laura A. Francis MBA | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 376 people. Revenue per employee of $534K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 20%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["SI-BONE, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.1B market cap on $201M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -110% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 87% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $9M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -8.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.22437673130193805},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 733% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"43,397 SiBone $SIBN Shares Sold by Sterling Capital Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/43397-sibone-sibn-shares-sold-by-sterling-capital-management-llc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793957591.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should Reaffirmed Revenue Outlook Require Action From SI BONE (SIBN) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-sibn/si-bone/news/should-reaffirmed-revenue-outlook-require-action-from-si-bon","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793928768.481,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Updates for SiBone (SIBN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/analysts-recent-ratings-updates-for-sibone-sibn.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906808.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SiBone (SIBN) Hit a 52 Week High, Can the Run Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024076/sibone-sibn-hit-a-52-week-high-can-the-run-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-52_week_high-3024076","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884508.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SiBone (NASDAQ:SIBN) Stock: Insider Jeffrey Dunn Sells 20,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/sibone-nasdaqsibn-stock-insider-jeffrey-dunn-sells-20000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793830170.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},